cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ck3agent in research, please cite it as below."
title: "ck3agent: an LLM agent that plays Crusader Kings III by steering the game's native AI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stebbins
    given-names: Harrison
version: 2026.10.0
# stamped at release; must match the release date
date-released: "2026-10-19"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3agent"
url: "https://github.com/skullbloc/ck3agent"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - game AI
  - Crusader Kings III
  - MCP
  - agents
abstract: >-
  ck3agent hooks Crusader Kings III's AI subsystem with an in-process bridge
  (LD_PRELOAD shared library) and exposes game state and steering through a
  Model Context Protocol server, so a language model can replace the game's
  strategic decision-making while the native AI executes. Released as a
  research tool with a Linux bridge pinned to one game build.
